invariant: INV-17
file: quic.c
catches: quic_driver_test
reason: ch_quic_open checks the level's range and neither the session
  state nor the read bit, so a failed session, which still stores the
  Initial connection ID for its close, opens the peer's Initial packets.
  test_close_after_failure seals one under the server's Initial key and
  requires the failed client to refuse it with CH_EINVAL.

--- old
    if (session_dead(q) || level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION ||
        (q->levels_ready & CH_QUIC_LEVEL_BIT(level, CH_KEY_READ)) == 0) {
--- new
    if (level > CH_LEVEL_APPLICATION) {
